From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ecm_classifier_dscp: keep a connection whose packets carry a mark off the NSS

A capture of one client's traffic on an access point needs that client's
connections on the CPU, where a packet socket sees them, and no other
client's. ECM's only per-connection veto without a PCC registrant is a
classifier's response, and the DSCP classifier is the one every
connection is offered, with conntrack or without (903).

A packet whose skb mark is ECM_CLASSIFIER_DSCP_NO_ACCEL_MARK (0x75360000,
set by a nftables rule on the client's frames in both directions) now
makes the classifier relevant and deny acceleration, before conntrack is
looked at. Nothing else about the connection is recorded: once its
packets no longer carry the mark, it is classified as before (the
no-conntrack path, the conntrack path, or not relevant and unassigned).
Its existing accelerated connections are decelerated by the capture
(defunct_by_mac); an accelerated packet never reaches the classifier.
Every packet without the mark takes exactly the path it took before.
---
--- a/ecm_classifier_dscp.c
+++ b/ecm_classifier_dscp.c
@@ -72,6 +72,13 @@
 #define ECM_CLASSIFIER_DSCP_PATH "net/ecm/ecm_classifier_dscp"
 
 /*
+ * The skb mark that keeps a connection off the NSS: a nftables rule sets
+ * it on the packets of one client whose traffic must reach the host (a
+ * capture). Its low byte is clear of ECM_INTERFACE_WIFI_QOS_TAG_MASK's tags.
+ */
+#define ECM_CLASSIFIER_DSCP_NO_ACCEL_MARK 0x75360000
+
+/*
  * struct ecm_classifier_dscp_instance
  * 	State to allow tracking of dynamic qos for a connection
  */
@@ -425,6 +432,21 @@
 	if (ECM_FRONT_END_ACCELERATION_NOT_POSSIBLE(accel_mode)) {
 		spin_lock_bh(&ecm_classifier_dscp_lock);
 		cdscpi->process_response.relevance = ECM_CLASSIFIER_RELEVANCE_NO;
+		goto dscp_classifier_out;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * A packet carrying the no-acceleration mark keeps its connection on
+	 * the CPU, with conntrack or without, for as long as its packets carry
+	 * it. Nothing else is recorded, so once they no longer do the
+	 * connection is classified as any other.
+	 */
+	if (skb->mark == ECM_CLASSIFIER_DSCP_NO_ACCEL_MARK) {
+		spin_lock_bh(&ecm_classifier_dscp_lock);
+		cdscpi->process_response.relevance = ECM_CLASSIFIER_RELEVANCE_YES;
+		cdscpi->process_response.became_relevant = ecm_db_time_get();
+		cdscpi->process_response.process_actions |= ECM_CLASSIFIER_PROCESS_ACTION_ACCEL_MODE;
+		cdscpi->process_response.accel_mode = ECM_CLASSIFIER_ACCELERATION_MODE_NO;
 		goto dscp_classifier_out;
 	}
 
